{"title":"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Video_Solution_by_Math_Is_Special)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Video Solution by Math Is Special)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be an integer greater than 1. For which real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/f/3bfc42ae1c0ab1d3125089680da5d224dc1a7313.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\lfloor nx \\rfloor - \\sum_{k=1}^{n} \\frac{\\lfloor kx \\rfloor}{k}\\]\" width=\"124\" height=\"48\" />\nmaximal, and what is the maximal value that this expression can take?\n</p><p>Note: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/6/d768692ac7e42f3377366c90d34a96e92fe1841e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor z \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"22\" height=\"19\" /> denotes the greatest integer less than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the given function be defined as:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/8/cc8c28318200fb9f265ac217760b6db8c7399de0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x) = \\lfloor nx \\rfloor - \\sum_{k=1}^{n} \\frac{\\lfloor kx \\rfloor}{k}\\]\" width=\"186\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>First, we show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is periodic with period 1. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/a/06a7fafb72bdeb1dea952e86f92b05d9b5272923.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = y + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />. Then:\n\\begin{align*}\nf(x+1) &amp;= \\lfloor n(x+1) \\rfloor - \\sum_{k=1}^n \\frac{\\lfloor k(x+1) \\rfloor}{k} \\\\\n&amp;= \\lfloor nx + n \\rfloor - \\sum_{k=1}^n \\frac{\\lfloor kx + k \\rfloor}{k} \\\\\n&amp;= \\lfloor nx \\rfloor + n - \\sum_{k=1}^n \\left( \\frac{\\lfloor kx \\rfloor}{k} + 1 \\right) \\\\\n&amp;= \\lfloor nx \\rfloor + n - \\sum_{k=1}^n \\frac{\\lfloor kx \\rfloor}{k} - n \\\\\n&amp;= f(x)\n\\end{align*}\nBecause of this periodicity, we can restrict our analysis to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/6/b46dd7848f1c0755d337bdd3ba7003ed18ec7cc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\in [0, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"73\" height=\"20\" /> and then generalize the result to all real numbers.\n</p><p>We partition the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/0/0004bfe2d7fa21b99eaf702d39b6de356c7915a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> subintervals of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/3/033fccb48ad772fa13dbc3e250499dd75feed7f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_m = \\left[\\frac{m}{n}, \\frac{m+1}{n}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"148\" height=\"45\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/c/3ec811d9a5d19ba7d1877f25643c83035bf2db44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = 0, 1, \\dots, n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/5/c65c29690c2e51d1b54c455d8c4445ced8042e84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\in I_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"17\" />. This implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/5/de537d5e6c9ac06d133cf021ff481ce8a48d2c53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\le nx &lt; m+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"135\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/9/279e44ab7418d8f2fa04580dc7435fce04e40039.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor nx \\rfloor = m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" />.&#160;\nAdditionally, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174dda36ef1764e8b5414074dc069d30745a68d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\ge \\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"56\" height=\"34\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/a/6da5c768d3e309c1b5337c06bf5ad8df078c5c01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f071ac601b1b611018c038f049c137116cef3c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$kx \\ge \\frac{km}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"76\" height=\"39\" />, which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/5/d152ea7e7b6ae7c8cd08f53294707855bd645402.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor kx \\rfloor \\ge \\left\\lfloor \\frac{km}{n} \\right\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"113\" height=\"45\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/3/1433a0cc182e25f18416a0555a9a64631eea0f0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\in \\{1, \\dots, n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"113\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/7/3574f000100115cdf6ddb6dfbff0b571046038f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor nx \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"20\" /> remains constant at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> throughout <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/6/396c1fe235363901de7c03e91dba166b80e3f753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> and the terms <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/1/b2155ea37268aa2f5662776e3f29a0e4c98b4ed4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor kx \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> are being subtracted, the maximum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/6/396c1fe235363901de7c03e91dba166b80e3f753.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"17\" /> is bounded above by its value at the lower endpoint:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/2/ef2ed688f6c380e86d0e0107132b454ad8673c69.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x) = m - \\sum_{k=1}^n \\frac{\\lfloor kx \\rfloor}{k} \\le m - \\sum_{k=1}^n \\frac{\\left\\lfloor \\dfrac{km}{n} \\right\\rfloor}{k} = f\\left(\\dfrac{m}{n}\\right)\\]\" width=\"388\" height=\"71\" />\nThis proves that the global maximum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/0/0004bfe2d7fa21b99eaf702d39b6de356c7915a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> must be attained at one of the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/8/1c89fe93d33e71e438484ca7ee13799038b42abf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"56\" height=\"34\" />.\n</p><p>We now evaluate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/0/1a0b74d41a9fbfb1dad3dfec35bb609fc27c26d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f\\left(\\dfrac mn\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"35\" />. Using the identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/b/c7b6b8799ae161f4774b6bdb15994397650bc23f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor z \\rfloor = z - \\{z\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"110\" height=\"20\" /> (where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/4/334a877ba8b21655eed0f8c85f3f592ec1729c24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{z\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"20\" /> is the fractional part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />), we get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/c/79c5f76081afdf04afb20c1bbf3d2ccec911a622.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f\\left(\\dfrac{m}{n}\\right) = m - \\sum_{k=1}^n \\dfrac{\\dfrac{km}{n} - \\left\\{\\dfrac{km}{n}\\right\\}}{k} = m - \\sum_{k=1}^n \\dfrac{m}{n} + \\sum_{k=1}^n \\frac{\\left\\{\\dfrac{km}{n}\\right\\}}{k}\\]\" width=\"479\" height=\"71\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/e/fdefa4a221140a7ed044eff1d8fb7b73e5e42bf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^n \\frac{m}{n} = m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"91\" height=\"53\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/e/5ce90b9568a4132432238c0a39e74d8d5bafd9a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\{\\frac{nm}{n}\\right\\} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"90\" height=\"35\" />, this simplifies beautifully to:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e335291bb39a655be4841e41ac033e59004b069a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f\\left(\\dfrac{m}{n}\\right) = \\sum_{k=1}^{n-1} \\frac{\\left\\{\\dfrac{km}{n}\\right\\}}{k} = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{k=1}^{n-1} \\frac{km \\bmod n}{k}\\]\" width=\"322\" height=\"71\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/f/d4f7dde0b254b37267dc235681fe25f91ee8fbcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_k = km \\bmod n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"17\" />. We want to find the integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/d/fad2f416eb8b788b91e6d66df4096cf1a9929d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\in \\{0, \\dots, n-1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"150\" height=\"20\" /> that maximizes the sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/d/a6de51ce2ae3b57a178a796f4e2b7f0704073a0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^{n-1} \\frac{c_k}{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"51\" height=\"56\" />.\n</p><p>We claim that the sum is strictly maximized when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/6/b96458057e208adbc1476240879778c20b61b049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"15\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/6/b96458057e208adbc1476240879778c20b61b049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"15\" />, the sequence becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/5/1f5e5ee3daf0f7f4ae1912554c8e29d0e72c6922.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_k = k(n-1) \\bmod n = -k \\bmod n = n-k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"336\" height=\"20\" />.&#160;\n</p><p>To prove that any other <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> yields a smaller sum, we compare the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/d/3bd87559f4e4c9af40246a0fdbafe6feab507414.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> with the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5aff5fb0471eccc876656b94481a2a2c7d68a886.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k = n-k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"17\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the multiset <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/4/8040bfed7978c4a84259d5281aaadd17db5ed324.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{c_1, \\dots, c_{n-1}\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"110\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/2/9a29705554d019e0a22e47f077cef8d18dba352f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1, 2, \\dots, n-1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"129\" height=\"20\" />.&#160;\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/6/e9637652da2e51c934b719ca8e7fecf5fca6b7a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = \\gcd(m, n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"20\" />. The multiset <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> consists of the multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/f/d6f5a3ab8d001f7db602fb3f0ba9148015c11c0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" />. Specifically, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> appears <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/9/6a9f2f925b6ad9c226b9ad118c60d88d4a8b6bd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> times, and each multiple <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/c/e3cdbf1413bdb6470c982039705e8b1defd214e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$vd$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> (for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c780d92d5afb550b6b4e23089277dcd7f106d83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"16\" />) appears <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times.&#160;\n</p><p>For any integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb88e7f8825db8c5d8dc5faacd8c66e32501330e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y \\in \\{1, \\dots, n-1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"144\" height=\"20\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/6/376d77429a175196387e4724da178007147a66c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_C(y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" /> be the number of elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> that are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/8/0787d58e5e66ea59985c5d95098af5fe1d8cca81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ge y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"17\" />. The elements <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/a/1aa01b2809f169d08e88f5c5689ace7487bee4f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$vd \\ge y \\implies v \\ge \\left\\lceil \\dfrac yd \\right\\rceil$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"170\" height=\"35\" />. The number of such valid multipliers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f23bf124b6b2b2a993eb313c72e678664ac74a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/a/2daae906578c763cf4514a6668d91a6ce7d16c89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{n}{d}-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"34\" /> is exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/7/1078d5bcfe6409be39ab7840d3f608e4325ed3ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{n}{d} - \\left\\lceil \\dfrac yd \\right\\rceil$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"71\" height=\"35\" />. Since each non-zero multiple appears <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times, we have:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/2/2421996dcb1cf18d42aaf5ed41ffbba2a07a4c78.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[N_C(y) = d \\left(\\frac{n}{d} - \\left\\lceil \\dfrac yd \\right\\rceil\\right) = n - d\\left\\lceil \\dfrac yd \\right\\rceil\\]\" width=\"274\" height=\"33\" />\nBecause <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/c/f4c18bf0b0e9b6e709822080a6a751690d2e9130.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d\\left\\lceil \\dfrac yd \\right\\rceil \\ge d\\left(\\dfrac yd\\right) = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"152\" height=\"35\" />, we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/9/ac91ffbb0b3544b07c275c66c42f818e9c814434.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_C(y) \\le n - y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"118\" height=\"20\" />. The number of elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> that are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/8/0787d58e5e66ea59985c5d95098af5fe1d8cca81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ge y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"17\" /> is precisely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/3/7d3d1a8ebe5147405dd975ec47a6dc7dc97be343.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_B(y) = n - y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"20\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/c/1ac5f040bf0704d6621720ca90b5cb0ea2fd3d32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_C(y) \\le N_B(y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"125\" height=\"20\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>This establishes that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />-th largest element of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/4/3b4cd01885cb569775f5d1143bc5139fff104bdc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\le$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />-th largest element of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> (which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/3/ca318ea13591cc525ed0841ab6c0fff917a6633c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-i$\" width=\"38\" height=\"12\" />). Consequently, for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/1/a719229c848756044a5426409fbd0cef67441435.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j \\in \\{1, \\dots, n-1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"142\" height=\"20\" />, the sum of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" /> elements of the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/d/3bd87559f4e4c9af40246a0fdbafe6feab507414.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> is bounded by the sum of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" /> largest elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, giving:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/9/c89521d31c8a5d75562e3edc7b69e86520661770.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=1}^j c_k \\le \\sum_{k=1}^j (n-k)\\]\" width=\"150\" height=\"51\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/7/9f774ab3ef1d5f42e0df637c8094d0d1dd77e9dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_j = \\sum_{k=1}^j (n-k - c_k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"168\" height=\"57\" />. We have proven that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/b/dbbd2ba25438b7b5e46c012c1af912391a0e7760.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_j \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"56\" height=\"19\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" />. Using summation by parts on our sum:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62fe141e23a490eca8bd1b21dcbd0787d1eefc90.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=1}^{n-1} \\frac{n-k - c_k}{k} = \\sum_{j=1}^{n-2} A_j \\left(\\frac{1}{j} - \\frac{1}{j+1}\\right) + A_{n-1} \\frac{1}{n-1}\\]\" width=\"402\" height=\"53\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/3/9f35738cd6d02318cf3be689cbc302eb220b88d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{j} - \\frac{1}{j+1} &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"114\" height=\"42\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/b/dbbd2ba25438b7b5e46c012c1af912391a0e7760.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_j \\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"56\" height=\"19\" />, the entire sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/9/aa9c151a661a687f6e3e9b6e95ff672c231b6ef3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ge 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" />. This implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/e/dae2d6bb3191c23ff7a6aa30e20b18bf1222cd4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=1}^{n-1} \\frac{c_k}{k} \\le \\sum_{k=1}^{n-1} \\frac{n-k}{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"151\" height=\"56\" />.&#160;\nEquality holds if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/3/0f30e221583be626323b2a3340577bd831601aab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_j = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"56\" height=\"19\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" />, meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/a/d3ac1030e7b1b0a962b6ca4ba90ee2408940d189.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_k = n-k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"17\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, which occurs only when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/c/9cca5d60e9383a5e46b45aa0d110518f77909f7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_1 = m = n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/6/b96458057e208adbc1476240879778c20b61b049.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"15\" /> is the unique maximizer among our interval lower bounds, the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> evaluates to:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/2/2920133686ef0e46b1638b4f9be40793a5344250.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f\\left(\\frac{n-1}{n}\\right) = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{k=1}^{n-1} \\frac{n-k}{k} = \\sum_{k=1}^{n-1} \\frac{1}{k} - \\frac{n-1}{n} = \\sum_{k=1}^n \\frac{1}{k} - 1\\]\" width=\"436\" height=\"51\" />\n</p><p>To find the continuous values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> where this maximum is achieved, we inspect the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/4/4e420e981a6e85e6a4034b2a614db66277cb245d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_{n-1} = \\left[\\frac{n-1}{n}, 1\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"146\" height=\"45\" />. For any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> in this interval, and for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/0/810bc3b19926c7e47659a31b7a3e7d177f1fd281.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le k \\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"15\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/2/ab2e0c7153b4388590d58a8e95ad51e36b4c55c9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k - \\frac{k}{n} = k \\left(\\frac{n-1}{n}\\right) \\le kx &lt; k\\]\" width=\"235\" height=\"43\" />\nBecause <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/0/810bc3b19926c7e47659a31b7a3e7d177f1fd281.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le k \\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"15\" />, the term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/4/3d4fd6fd17ca63b9a4081962ca72129bde2703c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{k}{n} \\le 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"39\" />, meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/d/0ddc0ef48b90f1da6f544408109bd83e3762cbf8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k-1 \\le k - \\frac{k}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"115\" height=\"39\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/d/a9d39ed2be084a985f498b6ec1d387a861797e86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$kx \\in [k-1, k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"116\" height=\"20\" />, which locks <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/1/b2155ea37268aa2f5662776e3f29a0e4c98b4ed4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor kx \\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> firmly at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dc6fab4c2fdb4e9046030fbfdcf6ea721b05602.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />.&#160;\nComputing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> anywhere in this interval yields the constant maximum:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/b/4db2ca4b15643a8464d5f3ef56a70cf8e4b39b0b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x) = (n-1) - \\sum_{k=1}^n \\frac{k-1}{k} = (n-1) - \\sum_{k=1}^n \\left(1 - \\frac{1}{k}\\right) = \\sum_{k=1}^n \\frac{1}{k} - 1\\]\" width=\"512\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p><b>Conclusion:</b>\n</p><p>Accounting for the periodicity of 1 established in Step 1, the maximal value is sustained across all intervals shifted by integers.\n</p>\n<ul><li>Maximal value:</li></ul>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/b/59b261e1e98e12921e0d4e4e3756d6f414e4ee7f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=1}^n \\frac{1}{k} - 1\\]\" width=\"72\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<ul><li>Real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> that achieve this:&#160;</li></ul>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/f/9df9c354dfc0e8251abaa550eaa0ad3f7f9f832c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x \\in \\bigcup_{p \\in \\mathbb{Z}} \\left[p - \\frac{1}{n}, p\\right)\\]\" width=\"141\" height=\"50\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>After some manipulation (see Solution 1), let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/d/badd28e12e1860b9a8b0073347688f595442fb2f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in \\left[\\frac{m}{n}, \\frac{m+1}{n}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"136\" height=\"45\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/3/0639b31dd19ca64c2b1452c5e4e62fad88db00de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\in\\{0,1,2,\\ldots, n-1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"184\" height=\"20\" />. We proceed by maximizing\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/6/ff6922f1624dd164be074d05998bae00549c562b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(x)\\le f\\left(\\frac{m}{n}\\right)=\\frac{1}{n}\\sum_{k=1}^{n}\\frac{km\\bmod{n}}{k}\\]\" width=\"269\" height=\"48\" />\nThe maximal is clearly not achievable when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/2/2e275495e7e44d279fb3e5051b3a63115e79ead5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />. We assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/d/d6d24f1c424298291d233e0301800fc2076fae7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"16\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/8/f981cdb0c7b87601f707445c4c191fa107931417.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k=km\\bmod n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p><b>Case 1: </b><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/e/c8edce2e5c4fc23d616b9921bcb7cb84471f209c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(m,n)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>We note that:\n</p><p>1) For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/3/8e33f1fe0e781c2e7bdd35f4236fd05842192561.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i,j\\in\\{0,1,\\ldots,n-1\\}, i\\neq j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"221\" height=\"20\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/4/b04e5133ba8ba8dbdd2a03a9824511b249ba152e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i\\neq a_j \\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"61\" height=\"19\" />. To prove, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/7/df75892817422e3362d70b337561d56aa55be6e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i=a_j\\,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" /> , then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/1/6417a81ccd1430137b1a02f9036d4e593c2589a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i-a_j\\equiv m(i-j)\\equiv 0\\pmod{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"255\" height=\"20\" />, which yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/2/00251835eb6bf90a89fb44863112b33132201906.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"38\" height=\"16\" /> as a contradiction.\n</p><p>2) The sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/1/1a1ac581036379d943ed46bb90ff0a53f288b770.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_k=\\frac{1}{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"56\" height=\"38\" /> is strictly decreasing for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/7/af7edfd31ee1302a42e013bf1a5c523b777da8e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=1,2,\\ldots, n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" /> as the summation occurs. By Rearrangement Inequality, the summation obtains its maximal when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/3/5a387f42a07107ae98339aff89b0ebace2824eae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1&gt;a_2&gt;\\ldots &gt; a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"15\" />.&#160;\n</p><p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/4/4042ed1366c0e959e6a678c2a46e1a4a44e257f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k\\in\\{0,1,2,\\ldots, n-1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"186\" height=\"20\" />. The sole way for those numbers to be strictly decreasing is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/a/bca0c3f693b269cb7a54ff032710965b152dc2e1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n-1&gt;n-2&gt;\\ldots&gt;0\\]\" width=\"186\" height=\"13\" />\nIn the case of maximal, this forces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/f/6afdc037060e2fc128f2489039b47c4f0167920e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k=n-k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Thus,\n\\begin{gather*}\na_k\\equiv km\\equiv -k\\pmod{n}\\iff\\\\\nm\\equiv -1\\pmod{n}\n\\end{gather*}\nWe have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/6/af644ae994acd3a0a7d07b14d53601d1eeed4a77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"15\" />. This gives the maximal of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/a/aea23eafe1aff1dc1f44d41ff06bc615d38246bd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{n}\\sum_{k=1}^{n}\\frac{km\\bmod{n}}{k}\\le \\frac{1}{n}\\sum_{k=1}^{n}\\frac{n-k}{k}=\\sum_{k=2}^{n}\\frac{1}{k}\\]\" width=\"314\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p><b>Case 2: </b><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/7/c57d1504f8f4e4a24175c310c090dbf3e0302c7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(m,n)=d&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"145\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f934597afa043ddf86cab8ddd348f1717b28820b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=d\\cdot q, m=d\\cdot b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/5/da5ee460a1e743455122f43ceb10979d5708bd3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd{(q,b)}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"20\" />. We get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/8/b7848a75eb641809e8199935c04beba394707029.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k=km\\bmod{n}=d\\, (bk\\bmod{q})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"248\" height=\"20\" />. This gives a multiset of values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/bea4d576937a04ec200b1037fc8ee33e8f744cb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/3/b63a96b454a78bef767dc0a936fed88d6a8b7a82.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_k\\in\\bigl\\{\\underbrace{n-d, n-d,\\ldots, n-d}_{d\\text{&#39;s }n-d}, \\enspace\\underbrace{n-2d, n-2d,\\ldots, n-2d}_{d\\text{&#39;s }n-2d}\\enspace ,\\ldots,\\enspace \\underbrace{0, 0,\\ldots, 0}_{d\\text{&#39;s }0}\\bigr\\}\\]\" width=\"587\" height=\"41\" />\nBy Rearrangement Inequality, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e2d7de9edd3b126414da20cf447d5f07169765.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1^*\\ge a_2^*\\ge \\ldots \\ge a_n^*$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"149\" height=\"19\" /> be a rearrangement of the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> that yields the maximal. We have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/3/b63c49a40b7c4aa9e831d4602f85a54dbc510dcc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{n}\\sum_{k=1}^{n}\\frac{a_k}{k}\\le\\frac{1}{n}\\sum_{k=1}^{n}\\frac{a_k^*}{k}\\]\" width=\"157\" height=\"48\" />\nGenerally, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/3/833967fba19e80f8654f0087124d1fe4a1341b51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\le t\\le q, 1\\le s\\le d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"18\" />. For indices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/3/ff385424f73fd661b72e37bb50c92cdb5ad8922d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=(t-1)d+s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"128\" height=\"20\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/b/d3bf948c5dc2cb9ad3b11777543977aa588a3e4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k^*=n-td$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"93\" height=\"19\" />. Note that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/c/70c3ba9fe0744589cf8fc9740ef61f84907b4157.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_k^*=n-td\\le n-td+d-s=n-(t-1)d-s=n-k\\]\" width=\"443\" height=\"18\" />\nBut the equality holds if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/5/2455bcc12228bff7661ca27aca1aa7ecc0bcbf25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s=d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/1/811a351f34ef48502ec19417bde03b9b3d8d5778.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d\\nmid k\\implies a_k^* &lt; n-k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"171\" height=\"20\" />, which means the upper bound from <b>Case 1</b> is <b>not attainable</b> for <b>Case 2</b>:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/1/1b153f523091231f7219ba6a1a0b6bd66638f374.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{n}\\sum_{k=1}^{n}\\frac{a_k^*}{k} &lt; \\frac{1}{n}\\sum_{k=1}^{n}\\frac{n-k}{k}=\\sum_{k=2}^{n}\\frac{1}{k}\\]\" width=\"250\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, by our analysis from <b>Case 1</b>, the maximal is achieved when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/6/af644ae994acd3a0a7d07b14d53601d1eeed4a77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"84\" height=\"15\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/a/a2aae7a85991d10f4a0bf9f044025f40c3fb178a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{n}\\sum_{k=1}^{n}\\frac{km\\bmod{n}}{k}\\le\\sum_{k=2}^{n}\\frac{1}{k}\\]\" width=\"196\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>Furthermore, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/2/67221492a707326425c532949f3546dd35643b63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=1-\\frac{1}{n}+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"113\" height=\"38\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/e/3cec35309192f6a5db5ec21369f4a202505b25c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le c &lt; \\frac{1}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"82\" height=\"38\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/6/9c631a77b6d85291fd8b573e38c0cb6d9de726fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1\\le k\\left(c-\\frac{1}{n}\\right)&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"167\" height=\"45\" />, we have\n\\begin{align*}\nf(x)&amp;=\\lfloor nx\\rfloor -\\sum_{k=1}^{n}\\frac{\\lfloor kx\\rfloor}{k}\\\\\n&amp;=\\lfloor n-1+cn\\rfloor-\\sum_{k=1}^{n}\\frac{\\left\\lfloor k+k\\left(c-\\frac{1}{n}\\right)\\right\\rfloor}{k}\\\\\n&amp;=n-1-\\sum_{k=1}^{n}\\frac{k-1}{k}\\\\\n&amp;=\\sum_{k=2}^{n}\\frac{1}{k}\\\\\n\\end{align*}\nWe see that all real <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/f/68f13490d86b968f745b30d4a429f7d579f196f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in \\left[1-\\frac{1}{n}, 1\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"120\" height=\"45\" /> yields the maximal.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> has a period of 1. Thus, the real <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> that attains the maximal satisfies\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/5/d454cf1a2bb2c89f65ccd75ad00ebae9e1ce8ee9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x\\in\\bigcup_{j\\in\\mathbb{Z}}\\left[j-\\frac{1}{n}, \\, j\\right)\\]\" width=\"143\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p>~Pieandpi31415926535897932\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Video_Solution_by_Math_Is_Special.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Video_Solution_by_Math_Is_Special)\">Solution 3 (Video Solution by Math Is Special)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Video Solution by Math Is Special)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ISdTOPnwb4I\">https://youtu.be/ISdTOPnwb4I</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/x9L1g3LAq7k\">https://youtu.be/x9L1g3LAq7k</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO\" title=\"2026 USAMO\">2026 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2026\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2026 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017172147\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.069 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.088 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 894/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1283/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 55/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 32432/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   11.970      1 -total\n 57.04%    6.827      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 40.89%    4.895      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36111:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017172147 and revision id 293767. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}